{"id":"f3c00024279f1f115e7c2d8c6738214270a71adf","url":"https://pele.run/","title":"Pele · Mermaid diagrams as themeable SVG","site_name":"Zeli","source":"Hacker News · 24h最热","byline":null,"excerpt":"Pele is a lightweight open source library that renders Mermaid diagrams to SVG, themed with CSS variables.","content_html":"<DIV class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div id=\"top\"><nav aria-label=\"Documentation\"></nav><div><section aria-labelledby=\"how-it-works\"><header><h2 id=\"how-it-works\">How it works</h2></header><p>Write Mermaid syntax, Pele renders it to SVG. Try editing the example below.</p><div data-code-block=\"\" data-home-editor=\"mermaid\"><p><span>Mermaid</span><span></span></p><pre><code data-language=\"mermaid\"><span><span><span>flowchart</span> <span>TD</span></span></span><span><span>  <span>A</span><span>[</span><span>Mermaid text</span><span>]</span> <span>--&gt;</span> <span>B</span><span>{</span><span>Flowchart?</span><span>}</span></span></span><span><span>  <span>B</span> <span>--</span><span> Yes </span><span>--&gt;</span> <span>C</span><span>[</span><span>Pele</span><span>]</span></span></span><span><span>  <span>B</span> <span>--</span><span> No </span><span>--&gt;</span> <span>D</span><span>[</span><span>Mermaid</span><span>]</span></span></span><span><span>  <span>C</span> <span>--&gt;</span> <span>E</span><span>([</span><span>SVG</span><span>])</span></span></span><span><span>  <span>D</span> <span>--&gt;</span> <span>E</span></span></span></code></pre></div><p>Use CSS variables to set colors and fonts. Color changes apply without re-rendering.</p><div><div data-code-block=\"\" data-home-editor=\"css\"><p><span>CSS</span><span></span></p><pre><code data-language=\"css\"><span><span><span>.pele </span><span>{</span></span></span><span><span>  <span>--pele-bg</span><span>: </span><span>#fffcf0</span><span>;</span></span></span><span><span>  <span>--pele-fg</span><span>: </span><span>#100f0f</span><span>;</span></span></span><span><span>  <span>--pele-muted</span><span>: </span><span>#6f6e69</span><span>;</span></span></span><span><span>  <span>--pele-line</span><span>: </span><span>#100f0f</span><span>;</span></span></span><span><span>  <span>--pele-surface</span><span>: </span><span>#f2f0e5</span><span>;</span></span></span><span><span>  <span>--pele-surface-alt</span><span>: </span><span>#e6e4d9</span><span>;</span></span></span><span><span>  <span>--pele-border</span><span>: </span><span>#cecdc3</span><span>;</span></span></span><span><span><span>}</span></span></span></code></pre></div><div data-pele-theme=\"light\"><p><span>Pele</span></p><figure aria-label=\"Flowchart rendered by Pele in a light theme\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 298 212\" width=\"298\" height=\"212\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;--_bg:var(--pele-bg,#fff);--_fg:var(--pele-fg,#1f1f1f);--_m:var(--pele-muted,#6e6e6e);--_l:var(--pele-line,#1f1f1f);--_s:var(--pele-surface,#f3f3f3);--_a:var(--pele-surface-alt,#e6e6e6);--_b:var(--pele-border,#8a8a8a);--_c:var(--pele-accent,#5b7bd5);color:var(--_fg);--_r:var(--pele-radius,4px);--_fm:var(--pele-font-mono,monospace);font:16px sans-serif;letter-spacing:normal;word-spacing:normal;text-transform:none;direction:ltr;font-family:var(--pele-font,sans-serif)\" fill=\"var(--_fg)\" role=\"graphics-document document\" aria-roledescription=\"flowchart\"><g><g data-id=\"Themes\"><rect x=\"158.69\" y=\"8\" width=\"130.69\" height=\"196\" fill=\"var(--_a)\" fill-opacity=\"0.5\" stroke=\"var(--_b)\" style=\"rx:var(--_r)\" /><text fill=\"var(--_m)\" x=\"201.58\" y=\"33.6\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Themes</text></g></g><g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--_l)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><g data-id=\"L_A_B_0\"><path d=\"M110.69,108C134.69,108 134.69,72 158.69,72L191.69,72\" /><path d=\"M198.69,72L190.69,75.36L190.69,68.64Z\" fill=\"var(--_l)\" stroke=\"none\" /></g><g data-id=\"L_A_C_0\"><path d=\"M110.69,124C134.69,124 134.69,160 158.69,160L191.69,160\" /><path d=\"M198.69,160L190.69,163.36L190.69,156.64Z\" fill=\"var(--_l)\" stroke=\"none\" /></g></g><g><g data-id=\"A\" transform=\"translate(59.34,116)\"><rect x=\"-51.34\" y=\"-24\" width=\"102.69\" height=\"48\" fill=\"var(--_s)\" stroke=\"var(--_b)\" style=\"rx:var(--_r)\" /><text x=\"0\" y=\"5.6\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Variables</text></g><g data-id=\"B\" transform=\"translate(234.03,72)\"><rect x=\"-35.34\" y=\"-24\" width=\"70.69\" height=\"48\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"var(--_s)\" stroke=\"var(--_b)\" /><text x=\"0\" y=\"5.6\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Light</text></g><g data-id=\"C\" transform=\"translate(233.58,160)\"><rect x=\"-34.89\" y=\"-24\" width=\"69.78\" height=\"48\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"var(--_s)\" stroke=\"var(--_b)\" /><text x=\"0\" y=\"5.6\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dark</text></g></g></svg></figure></div></div></section><section aria-labelledby=\"why-pele\"><header><h2 id=\"why-pele\">Why Pele?</h2><p>Zero dependencies, 6× smaller, and up to 500× faster than Mermaid.js. Pele supports every diagram type built into Mermaid 12.1.0.</p></header><div role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"why-pele\" tabindex=\"0\"><table><thead><tr><td></td><th scope=\"col\">Pele</th><th scope=\"col\">Mermaid.js</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bundle size <small>gzip</small></td><td>230 kB</td><td>1.6 MB</td></tr><tr><td>Render time</td><td>0.05–0.3 ms</td><td>6–82 ms</td></tr><tr><td>Direct dependencies</td><td>0</td><td>23</td></tr><tr><td>Small screens</td><td>Adapts the layout</td><td>Scales the diagram</td></tr><tr><td>Theming</td><td>CSS variables</td><td>Theme configuration</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section aria-labelledby=\"install-title\"><header><h2 id=\"install-title\">Pele in your app</h2></header><p>Add Pele to your app using the <a href=\"/api\">API</a>.</p><div id=\"install-npm\" data-install-panel=\"npm\"><figure data-code-block=\"\"><span></span><pre><code data-language=\"shell\"><span><span><span>npm</span> install pele</span></span></code></pre></figure></div><p>Pass Mermaid syntax to <code>render()</code> and insert the returned SVG into your page.</p><figure data-code-block=\"\"><span></span><pre><code data-language=\"ts\"><span><span><span>import</span> <span>{</span> <span>render</span> <span>}</span> <span>from</span> <span>'</span><span>pele</span><span>'</span><span>;</span></span></span><span><span></span></span><span><span><span>const</span> <span>{</span> <span>svg</span> <span>}</span> <span>=</span> <span>render</span><span>(</span><span>`</span><span>flowchart LR</span></span></span><span><span><span>  A[Mermaid text] --&gt; B[SVG]</span><span>`</span><span>)</span><span>;</span></span></span><span><span></span></span><span><span><span>document</span><span>.</span><span>querySelector</span><span>(</span><span>'</span><span>#diagram</span><span>'</span><span>)</span><span>.</span><span>innerHTML</span> <span>=</span> <span>svg</span><span>;</span></span></span></code></pre></figure></section><section aria-labelledby=\"explore-title\"><header><h2 id=\"explore-title\">Explore</h2></header><nav aria-label=\"Documentation\"><a href=\"/examples\"><h3>Examples</h3><p>Browse supported diagram types.</p></a><a href=\"/api\"><h3>API</h3><p>Render diagrams in your app.</p></a><a href=\"/theming\"><h3>Theming</h3><p>Set colors and fonts with CSS variables.</p></a><a href=\"/compatibility\"><h3>Compatibility</h3><p>Compare syntax, layout, and features with Mermaid.</p></a></nav></section><section aria-labelledby=\"pele-in-use\"><header><P><h2 id=\"pele-in-use\">Pele in use</h2></P><p>Pele is <a href=\"https://github.com/obsidianmd/pele\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">open source</a>, developed for <a href=\"https://obsidian.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Obsidian</a> to render diagrams quickly and match your theme. It is named after <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pele_(deity)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pele</a>, the goddess of volcanoes and fire.</p></header></section></div></div></DIV>","content_text":"How it worksWrite Mermaid syntax, Pele renders it to SVG. Try editing the example below.Mermaidflowchart TD A[Mermaid text] --> B{Flowchart?} B -- Yes --> C[Pele] B -- No --> D[Mermaid] C --> E([SVG]) D --> EUse CSS variables to set colors and fonts. Color changes apply without re-rendering.CSS.pele { --pele-bg: #fffcf0; --pele-fg: #100f0f; --pele-muted: #6f6e69; --pele-line: #100f0f; --pele-surface: #f2f0e5; --pele-surface-alt: #e6e4d9; --pele-border: #cecdc3;}PeleThemesVariablesLightDarkWhy Pele?Zero dependencies, 6× smaller, and up to 500× faster than Mermaid.js. Pele supports every diagram type built into Mermaid 12.1.0.PeleMermaid.jsBundle size gzip230 kB1.6 MBRender time0.05–0.3 ms6–82 msDirect dependencies023Small screensAdapts the layoutScales the diagramThemingCSS variablesTheme configurationPele in your appAdd Pele to your app using the API.npm install pelePass Mermaid syntax to render() and insert the returned SVG into your page.import { render } from 'pele';const { svg } = render(`flowchart LR A[Mermaid text] --> B[SVG]`);document.querySelector('#diagram').innerHTML = svg;ExploreExamplesBrowse supported diagram types.APIRender diagrams in your app.ThemingSet colors and fonts with CSS variables.CompatibilityCompare syntax, layout, and features with Mermaid.Pele in usePele is open source, developed for Obsidian to render diagrams quickly and match your theme. It is named after Pele, the goddess of volcanoes and fire.","fetched_at":"2026-10-18T08:36:58.081Z","ok":true,"blocks":[{"html_en":"<h2 id=\"how-it-works\">How it works</h2>","sentences":[{"en":"How it works","zh":"它是如何运作的"}]},{"html_en":"<p>Write Mermaid syntax, Pele renders it to SVG. Try editing the example below.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"Write Mermaid syntax, Pele renders it to SVG.","zh":null},{"en":"Try editing the example below.","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p><span>Mermaid</span><span></span></p>","sentences":[{"en":"Mermaid","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<